{"events":[{"tStartMs":2040,"dDurationMs":3840,"segs":[{"utf8":"This video was made possible by CuriosityStream."}]},{"tStartMs":5880,"dDurationMs":4920,"segs":[{"utf8":"Watch thousands of high-quality documentaries and get access to my streaming service, Nebula"}]},{"tStartMs":10800,"dDurationMs":1410,"segs":[{"utf8":"using the link in the description."}]},{"tStartMs":12210,"dDurationMs":6350,"segs":[{"utf8":"In 1940, a team of American explorers set out to chart one of the last unexplored corners"}]},{"tStartMs":18560,"dDurationMs":5440,"segs":[{"utf8":"of the planet, traveling thousands of kilometers to reach the South Pole, through parts of"}]},{"tStartMs":24000,"dDurationMs":2890,"segs":[{"utf8":"Antarctica no human had ever seen before."}]},{"tStartMs":26890,"dDurationMs":6490,"segs":[{"utf8":"A place so remote and inhospitable, many earlier attempts to explore it had either failed or"}]},{"tStartMs":33380,"dDurationMs":1710,"segs":[{"utf8":"ended in tragedy."}]},{"tStartMs":35090,"dDurationMs":4500,"segs":[{"utf8":"But unlike earlier attempts, the Americans will explore Antarctica with the ultimate"}]},{"tStartMs":39590,"dDurationMs":2410,"segs":[{"utf8":"exploration machine."}]},{"tStartMs":42000,"dDurationMs":5630,"segs":[{"utf8":"A 37 ton mobile base which will sustain a small team of explorers while they live, work"}]},{"tStartMs":47630,"dDurationMs":4070,"segs":[{"utf8":"and sleep in isolation for an entire year."}]},{"tStartMs":51700,"dDurationMs":2530,"segs":[{"utf8":"This is the Antarctic Snow Cruiser."}]},{"tStartMs":54230,"dDurationMs":2470,"segs":[{"utf8":"Designed to push through the harshest conditions on the planet."}]},{"tStartMs":56700,"dDurationMs":15000,"segs":[{"utf8":"And it’ll end up as one of history’s greatest engineering legends."}]},{"tStartMs":71700,"dDurationMs":5690,"segs":[{"utf8":"Before 1939, only two expedition teams had ever set foot on the South Pole."}]},{"tStartMs":77390,"dDurationMs":2830,"segs":[{"utf8":"And only one of them made it back out alive."}]},{"tStartMs":80220,"dDurationMs":5030,"segs":[{"utf8":"Because temperatures in Antarctica can fall below -80 degrees Celsius."}]},{"tStartMs":85250,"dDurationMs":5370,"segs":[{"utf8":"Winds of two or even three hundred kilometers an hour are not unheard of. And with over"}]},{"tStartMs":90620,"dDurationMs":4920,"segs":[{"utf8":"14 million square kilometers of icefields and polar mountains, it’s an environment"}]},{"tStartMs":95540,"dDurationMs":2230,"segs":[{"utf8":"unfit for human life."}]},{"tStartMs":97770,"dDurationMs":5150,"segs":[{"utf8":"But underneath the frozen landscape lies the potential for enormous riches, including vast"}]},{"tStartMs":102920,"dDurationMs":2210,"segs":[{"utf8":"oil and mineral reserves."}]},{"tStartMs":105130,"dDurationMs":5890,"segs":[{"utf8":"And by 1939, the World’s powers had begun claiming huge portions of it for themselves."}]},{"tStartMs":111020,"dDurationMs":4320,"segs":[{"utf8":"But missing from this map of Antarctic claims was the United States."}]},{"tStartMs":115340,"dDurationMs":5550,"segs":[{"utf8":"While American explorers had made inroads into the continent, these were privately-funded"}]},{"tStartMs":120890,"dDurationMs":1000,"segs":[{"utf8":"expeditions."}]},{"tStartMs":121890,"dDurationMs":4340,"segs":[{"utf8":"To make their own claim on Antarctica, the United States would need a larger and more"}]},{"tStartMs":126230,"dDurationMs":1529,"segs":[{"utf8":"official presence."}]},{"tStartMs":127759,"dDurationMs":6661,"segs":[{"utf8":"So in 1939, U.S. President Roosevelt launched the United States Antarctic Service Expedition."}]},{"tStartMs":134420,"dDurationMs":4370,"segs":[{"utf8":"In the fall of that year, two ships, carrying one hundred and twenty five men, would set"}]},{"tStartMs":138790,"dDurationMs":4509,"segs":[{"utf8":"sail for Antarctica in the largest American expedition to date."}]},{"tStartMs":143299,"dDurationMs":5041,"segs":[{"utf8":"Their mission would be to explore previously unknown regions of the continent and to establish"}]},{"tStartMs":148340,"dDurationMs":3579,"segs":[{"utf8":"two new field bases on either side of Antarctica."}]},{"tStartMs":151919,"dDurationMs":5311,"segs":[{"utf8":"The expedition would bring a host of exploration equipment, but the centerpiece would be the"}]},{"tStartMs":157230,"dDurationMs":2039,"segs":[{"utf8":"Antarctic Snow Cruiser."}]},{"tStartMs":159269,"dDurationMs":2411,"segs":[{"utf8":"Nothing like it had ever been built before."}]},{"tStartMs":161680,"dDurationMs":5440,"segs":[{"utf8":"The size of a small building, and would even carry its own aircraft along with five explorers"}]},{"tStartMs":167120,"dDurationMs":3339,"segs":[{"utf8":"who would live and work onboard it for up to a year."}]},{"tStartMs":170459,"dDurationMs":2241,"segs":[{"utf8":"The Snow Cruiser would have a special role."}]},{"tStartMs":172700,"dDurationMs":4489,"segs":[{"utf8":"It’s crew would travel thousands of kilometers to reach the South Pole."}]},{"tStartMs":177189,"dDurationMs":4380,"segs":[{"utf8":"From there, they’d continue Eastwards to the newly established American field base."}]},{"tStartMs":181569,"dDurationMs":4560,"segs":[{"utf8":"In effect laying the groundwork for an American claim on the continent."}]},{"tStartMs":186129,"dDurationMs":4711,"segs":[{"utf8":"News of the expedition made the headlines, but it was the Antarctic Snow Cruiser and"}]},{"tStartMs":190840,"dDurationMs":9530,"segs":[{"utf8":"it’s daring mission that would capture the world's imagination."}]},{"tStartMs":200370,"dDurationMs":4640,"segs":[{"utf8":"Designed by Chicago's Armour Institute of Technology, the Antarctic Snow Cruiser looked"}]},{"tStartMs":205010,"dDurationMs":2789,"segs":[{"utf8":"like something out of a Jules Verne novel."}]},{"tStartMs":207799,"dDurationMs":6190,"segs":[{"utf8":"To traverse the rough polar landscape, engineers give it enormous ten foot tall rubber wheels,"}]},{"tStartMs":213989,"dDurationMs":3560,"segs":[{"utf8":"which would help absorb the shock of the unforgiving frozen terrain."}]},{"tStartMs":217549,"dDurationMs":5851,"segs":[{"utf8":"When faced with a seemingly impassable ice crevasse, the Cruiser would hydraulically"}]},{"tStartMs":223400,"dDurationMs":5069,"segs":[{"utf8":"retract its wheels and use it’s large front and rear overhangs to slide over gaps."}]},{"tStartMs":228469,"dDurationMs":4610,"segs":[{"utf8":"Allowing it to cross ice crevices up to four and half meters wide."}]},{"tStartMs":233079,"dDurationMs":5650,"segs":[{"utf8":"To travel reliability for months on end, the Cruiser would feature an innovative diesel-electric"}]},{"tStartMs":238729,"dDurationMs":1940,"segs":[{"utf8":"hybrid drivetrain."}]},{"tStartMs":240669,"dDurationMs":4761,"segs":[{"utf8":"Instead of driving the Cruiser directly, diesel engines would supply power to electric motors"}]},{"tStartMs":245430,"dDurationMs":2039,"segs":[{"utf8":"inside each wheel hub."}]},{"tStartMs":247469,"dDurationMs":5720,"segs":[{"utf8":"This space saving design would do away with the need for complex driveshafts and gearboxes,"}]},{"tStartMs":253189,"dDurationMs":2410,"segs":[{"utf8":"promising to be more reliable."}]},{"tStartMs":255599,"dDurationMs":4191,"segs":[{"utf8":"To combat frigid temperatures, coolant from the engines would circulate throughout the"}]},{"tStartMs":259790,"dDurationMs":6290,"segs":[{"utf8":"cabin to heat interior spaces, and in extreme weather, coolant could also heat the Cruiser’s"}]},{"tStartMs":266080,"dDurationMs":2090,"segs":[{"utf8":"hydraulically retracted wheels."}]},{"tStartMs":268170,"dDurationMs":4780,"segs":[{"utf8":"The Antarctic Snow Cruiser would carry enough fuel, food and supplies to last an entire"}]},{"tStartMs":272950,"dDurationMs":1000,"segs":[{"utf8":"year."}]},{"tStartMs":273950,"dDurationMs":3550,"segs":[{"utf8":"And feature spaces for it’s five explorers to live, sleep and work."}]},{"tStartMs":277500,"dDurationMs":5280,"segs":[{"utf8":"It would even carry it’s own biplane to conduct aerial surveys and photograph hundreds"}]},{"tStartMs":282780,"dDurationMs":2650,"segs":[{"utf8":"of kilometers of Antarctic territory."}]},{"tStartMs":285430,"dDurationMs":5250,"segs":[{"utf8":"With the Snow Cruiser, the Americans would explore more of Antarctica in just a few months"}]},{"tStartMs":290680,"dDurationMs":3190,"segs":[{"utf8":"than all previous expeditions combined."}]},{"tStartMs":293870,"dDurationMs":7540,"segs":[{"utf8":"When the Cruiser rolled out it’s assembly plant on October 24, 1939, huge crowds formed"}]},{"tStartMs":301410,"dDurationMs":1440,"segs":[{"utf8":"to greet it."}]},{"tStartMs":302850,"dDurationMs":2470,"segs":[{"utf8":"But things were about to unravel."}]},{"tStartMs":305320,"dDurationMs":6110,"segs":[{"utf8":"Although research and design of the Snow Cruiser started in 1937, it wasn't until the spring"}]},{"tStartMs":311430,"dDurationMs":4660,"segs":[{"utf8":"of 1939 that a decision was made to use it in the upcoming expedition."}]},{"tStartMs":316090,"dDurationMs":5000,"segs":[{"utf8":"That left just six months to finish design and construction, forcing engineers to work"}]},{"tStartMs":321090,"dDurationMs":1000,"segs":[{"utf8":"around the clock."}]},{"tStartMs":322090,"dDurationMs":4850,"segs":[{"utf8":"And the Cruiser rolled out of its assembly plant in Chicago just weeks before it had"}]},{"tStartMs":326940,"dDurationMs":5120,"segs":[{"utf8":"to be loaded onto expedition ships waiting in Boston, leaving little time to test the"}]},{"tStartMs":332060,"dDurationMs":1740,"segs":[{"utf8":"machine’s capabilities."}]},{"tStartMs":333800,"dDurationMs":6010,"segs":[{"utf8":"Instead the Cruiser would be driven 1,600 kilometers all the way from Chicago to Boston in a shakedown"}]},{"tStartMs":339810,"dDurationMs":2350,"segs":[{"utf8":"trip to work out any issues."}]},{"tStartMs":342160,"dDurationMs":5080,"segs":[{"utf8":"With all the excitement and press, the cross-country trip would become a national sensation."}]},{"tStartMs":347240,"dDurationMs":3600,"segs":[{"utf8":"But it would also prove to be more difficult than anyone anticipated."}]},{"tStartMs":350840,"dDurationMs":5060,"segs":[{"utf8":"In Fort Wayne, Indiana, just a few days into the journey, progress was halted by of all"}]},{"tStartMs":355900,"dDurationMs":1600,"segs":[{"utf8":"things, heavy rains."}]},{"tStartMs":357500,"dDurationMs":2670,"segs":[{"utf8":"Which made roads too slippery to continue."}]},{"tStartMs":360170,"dDurationMs":5960,"segs":[{"utf8":"Soon after, the Cruiser lost control and careened into a ditch, where crews spent the next three"}]},{"tStartMs":366130,"dDurationMs":2200,"segs":[{"utf8":"days trying to get it unstuck."}]},{"tStartMs":368330,"dDurationMs":5140,"segs":[{"utf8":"It was an embarrassing start for a supposedly unstoppable machine, designed to handle the"}]},{"tStartMs":373470,"dDurationMs":2360,"segs":[{"utf8":"most difficult terrain on earth."}]},{"tStartMs":375830,"dDurationMs":4640,"segs":[{"utf8":"A hydraulic line failure and a small fender bender further delayed progress."}]},{"tStartMs":380470,"dDurationMs":5740,"segs":[{"utf8":"But worst of all was the realization of just how painfully slow the Cruiser was."}]},{"tStartMs":386210,"dDurationMs":4020,"segs":[{"utf8":"It should have been able to travel at speeds of up to 48 kilometers per hour."}]},{"tStartMs":390230,"dDurationMs":3060,"segs":[{"utf8":"But it struggled to reach even a fraction of that."}]},{"tStartMs":393290,"dDurationMs":4730,"segs":[{"utf8":"The problem was, each of it’s electric wheel hub motors produced just 75 horsepower."}]},{"tStartMs":398020,"dDurationMs":5900,"segs":[{"utf8":"It meant that altogether the 37 ton Cruiser had just 8 horsepower per ton to motivate"}]},{"tStartMs":403920,"dDurationMs":1350,"segs":[{"utf8":"it forward."}]},{"tStartMs":405270,"dDurationMs":3840,"segs":[{"utf8":"And wherever the slow moving machine went, it backed up traffic."}]},{"tStartMs":409110,"dDurationMs":3620,"segs":[{"utf8":"Outside of Boston, it caused the world’s worst traffic jam."}]},{"tStartMs":412730,"dDurationMs":2490,"segs":[{"utf8":"Backing up 70,000 cars."}]},{"tStartMs":415220,"dDurationMs":5830,"segs":[{"utf8":"But on November 12, the cruiser finally arrived in Boston with just 2 days to spare."}]},{"tStartMs":421050,"dDurationMs":2980,"segs":[{"utf8":"The drive was supposed to have taken 8 days."}]},{"tStartMs":424030,"dDurationMs":2430,"segs":[{"utf8":"Instead it took nearly 3 weeks."}]},{"tStartMs":426460,"dDurationMs":5130,"segs":[{"utf8":"The Cruiser struggled so much on smooth paved highways, many questioned whether it was really"}]},{"tStartMs":431590,"dDurationMs":1320,"segs":[{"utf8":"ready for the expedition."}]},{"tStartMs":432910,"dDurationMs":4700,"segs":[{"utf8":"But with so much excitement and publicity, there was no turning back."}]},{"tStartMs":437610,"dDurationMs":6140,"segs":[{"utf8":"On November 15, 1939 the most ambitious American expedition left for Antarctica."}]},{"tStartMs":443750,"dDurationMs":9950,"segs":[{"utf8":"But for the Snow Cruiser, things were about to turn from bad to ugly."}]},{"tStartMs":453700,"dDurationMs":5440,"segs":[{"utf8":"The mishaps would continue as soon as the Cruiser landed in Antarctica.Because the machine’s"}]},{"tStartMs":459140,"dDurationMs":2670,"segs":[{"utf8":"real problems, were only just beginning"}]},{"tStartMs":461810,"dDurationMs":5100,"segs":[{"utf8":"Having been built in only 11 weeks over a single midwestern summer, the Antarctic Snow"}]},{"tStartMs":466910,"dDurationMs":3950,"segs":[{"utf8":"Cruiser would see snow for the very first time in January of 1940."}]},{"tStartMs":470860,"dDurationMs":3570,"segs":[{"utf8":"And immediately it looked out of its element."}]},{"tStartMs":474430,"dDurationMs":6430,"segs":[{"utf8":"While the Cruiser had proven itself on highways, on tough uneven terrain, the machine was hopelessly"}]},{"tStartMs":480860,"dDurationMs":1279,"segs":[{"utf8":"underpowered."}]},{"tStartMs":482139,"dDurationMs":2421,"segs":[{"utf8":"But the real problem were the tires."}]},{"tStartMs":484560,"dDurationMs":5060,"segs":[{"utf8":"Designed to absorb impacts and to be virtually indestructible, they were also..perfectly"}]},{"tStartMs":489620,"dDurationMs":1000,"segs":[{"utf8":"smooth."}]},{"tStartMs":490620,"dDurationMs":3019,"segs":[{"utf8":"And in the Antarctic snow, they spun hopelessly."}]},{"tStartMs":493639,"dDurationMs":4791,"segs":[{"utf8":"Meaning a machine built to conquer mountain ranges, could barely move an inch"}]},{"tStartMs":498430,"dDurationMs":3830,"segs":[{"utf8":"The decision to use smooth tires is perplexing in hindsight."}]},{"tStartMs":502260,"dDurationMs":4110,"segs":[{"utf8":"But with such a tight development timeline, engineers had to make due with an already"}]},{"tStartMs":506370,"dDurationMs":4769,"segs":[{"utf8":"existing tire design specifically built for swamp buggies."}]},{"tStartMs":511139,"dDurationMs":3060,"segs":[{"utf8":"Cutting threads into the tires might have been possible."}]},{"tStartMs":514199,"dDurationMs":3780,"segs":[{"utf8":"But designers figured they’d just fill up with ice and snow anyway."}]},{"tStartMs":517979,"dDurationMs":4011,"segs":[{"utf8":"Not that they had time to test the theory in actual ice or snow."}]},{"tStartMs":521990,"dDurationMs":5009,"segs":[{"utf8":"In a desperate effort to solve traction problems, crews attached chains to the tires and even"}]},{"tStartMs":526999,"dDurationMs":2380,"segs":[{"utf8":"doubled up the front wheels with spares."}]},{"tStartMs":529379,"dDurationMs":2001,"segs":[{"utf8":"But it made little difference."}]},{"tStartMs":531380,"dDurationMs":4079,"segs":[{"utf8":"After weeks of struggling, it was obvious that part of the problem was the machine’s"}]},{"tStartMs":535459,"dDurationMs":2240,"segs":[{"utf8":"unequal weight distribution."}]},{"tStartMs":537699,"dDurationMs":4401,"segs":[{"utf8":"Driving the Cruiser backwards actually turned out to be the most effective way to get it"}]},{"tStartMs":542100,"dDurationMs":1000,"segs":[{"utf8":"moving."}]},{"tStartMs":543100,"dDurationMs":1510,"segs":[{"utf8":"So that’s what they did."}]},{"tStartMs":544610,"dDurationMs":5360,"segs":[{"utf8":"On its longest trek the Cruiser managed to travel backwards for 148 kilometres in a loop"}]},{"tStartMs":549970,"dDurationMs":1839,"segs":[{"utf8":"around the landing base."}]},{"tStartMs":551809,"dDurationMs":4111,"segs":[{"utf8":"But driving in reverse severely limited the Cruiser’s speed."}]},{"tStartMs":555920,"dDurationMs":5159,"segs":[{"utf8":"And there was no way it could make it all the way to the south pole in reverse."}]},{"tStartMs":561079,"dDurationMs":5200,"segs":[{"utf8":"The expedition team eventually admitted defeat and permanently parked the Cruiser for use"}]},{"tStartMs":566279,"dDurationMs":4331,"segs":[{"utf8":"as a stationary laboratory."}]},{"tStartMs":570610,"dDurationMs":5479,"segs":[{"utf8":"The expedition would continue without the Cruiser, but it would also have to end early."}]},{"tStartMs":576089,"dDurationMs":4582,"segs":[{"utf8":"With the Second World War looming, the entire project was abandoned and the expedition team"}]},{"tStartMs":580671,"dDurationMs":1819,"segs":[{"utf8":"returned home."}]},{"tStartMs":582490,"dDurationMs":5889,"segs":[{"utf8":"After the War, the world had changed and conquest and colonization of distant lands had fallen"}]},{"tStartMs":588379,"dDurationMs":1500,"segs":[{"utf8":"out of favour."}]},{"tStartMs":589879,"dDurationMs":5121,"segs":[{"utf8":"The abandoned Snow Cruiser was last spotted in 1958, after it was dug out from under several"}]},{"tStartMs":595000,"dDurationMs":1180,"segs":[{"utf8":"meters of snow."}]},{"tStartMs":596180,"dDurationMs":2610,"segs":[{"utf8":"Today, the machine’s whereabouts are unknown."}]},{"tStartMs":598790,"dDurationMs":4659,"segs":[{"utf8":"It’s either still buried under sheets of ice, or has since broken off on an ice flow"}]},{"tStartMs":603449,"dDurationMs":1731,"segs":[{"utf8":"and sunk to the bottom of the ocean."}]},{"tStartMs":605180,"dDurationMs":5390,"segs":[{"utf8":"In the end, the Antarctic Snow Cruiser had clearly been rushed into service and the result"}]},{"tStartMs":610570,"dDurationMs":4759,"segs":[{"utf8":"was a machine that had been over designed and under-tested."}]},{"tStartMs":615329,"dDurationMs":7781,"segs":[{"utf8":"Extreme optimism had seemingly been its design philosophy."}]},{"tStartMs":623110,"dDurationMs":4430,"segs":[{"utf8":"This is the SR-71 Blackbird, the world’s fastest jet."}]},{"tStartMs":627540,"dDurationMs":5469,"segs":[{"utf8":"For years, the Blackbird could operate anywhere in the world using speed to outrun any threat."}]},{"tStartMs":633009,"dDurationMs":5601,"segs":[{"utf8":"But the legendary spy plane would eventually meet its match."}]},{"tStartMs":638610,"dDurationMs":2289,"segs":[{"utf8":"This is the MiG-31."}]},{"tStartMs":640899,"dDurationMs":5230,"segs":[{"utf8":"Designed to intercept any threat. It's one of the fastest combat jets to enter into service"}]},{"tStartMs":646129,"dDurationMs":3020,"segs":[{"utf8":"and holds the absolute world record for altitude."}]},{"tStartMs":649149,"dDurationMs":4690,"segs":[{"utf8":"It’s phased array radar can track multiple targets hundreds of kilometers away."}]},{"tStartMs":653839,"dDurationMs":6920,"segs":[{"utf8":"And just four MiG-31s can defend an area of airspace nearly a thousand kilometres wide."}]},{"tStartMs":660759,"dDurationMs":5651,"segs":[{"utf8":"In a few weeks, I’ll be releasing my next Nebula-exclusive on the legendary MiG-31 Foxhound."}]},{"tStartMs":666410,"dDurationMs":6020,"segs":[{"utf8":"It’s just one of a growing number of exclusive Mustard videos on Nebula."}]},{"tStartMs":672430,"dDurationMs":4969,"segs":[{"utf8":"Nebula is where Youtube’s top educational creators upload videos everyday, and it’s"}]},{"tStartMs":677399,"dDurationMs":4021,"segs":[{"utf8":"where you can enjoy videos without advertisements or sponsor messages."}]},{"tStartMs":681420,"dDurationMs":4409,"segs":[{"utf8":"The best part about Nebula is that it’s free when you sign up for CuriosityStream."}]},{"tStartMs":685829,"dDurationMs":4341,"segs":[{"utf8":"A streaming service with thousands of big budget award-winning documentaries."}]},{"tStartMs":690170,"dDurationMs":4950,"segs":[{"utf8":"If you want to learn more about the fascinating history of Antarctic exploration, check out"}]},{"tStartMs":695120,"dDurationMs":4950,"segs":[{"utf8":"Icemen: 200 years in Antarctica and learn why so many have been drawn to the frozen"}]},{"tStartMs":700070,"dDurationMs":1709,"segs":[{"utf8":"deadly abyss."}]},{"tStartMs":701779,"dDurationMs":5241,"segs":[{"utf8":"Get an entire year of both CuriosityStream and Nebula for less than $15 by going to"}]},{"tStartMs":707020,"dDurationMs":5640,"segs":[{"utf8":"curiositystream.com/mustard and use the promo code ‘mustard’ when you sign up."}]}]}